<!-- wp:doclap/faq-list {"anchor":"faq","introLabelStyle":"eyebrow","showFilters":false,"showQuestionCount":false,"asideLabel":"06 / BEFORE WE BEGIN","asideHeading":"A few things,<br>made clear.","asideCopy":"Good collaboration begins with a little clarity. Here are some useful starting points.","asideLinkLabel":"All questions","asideLinkUrl":"/faqs-2/","questions":[{"category":"","question":"What kind of projects are a good fit?","answer":"Expressive websites, portfolio experiences and thoughtful motion-led interfaces. The right starting point is a clear problem and a shared commitment to craft."},{"category":"","question":"How is a project priced?","answer":"Scope, complexity and the level of design and development determine the proposal. Pricing is agreed before work begins; no unconfirmed rates are published here."},{"category":"","question":"Can we work together beyond launch?","answer":"Yes. Ongoing collaboration can cover new pages, motion refinements and further development. The scope and working rhythm are agreed together."},{"category":"","question":"How do you approach animation and accessibility?","answer":"Motion supports hierarchy and interaction rather than distracting from them. Keyboard navigation, visible focus and reduced-motion preferences are part of the experience."},{"category":"","question":"Are the team and testimonials on this page real?","answer":"The team section describes disciplines, not a published staff roster. Testimonial cards are explicitly labeled layout previews, with no invented clients, ratings or endorsements."}]} /-->
